      "content": "That makes sense—focusing on the actual impact rather than the intent. \n\nBut what about the cases where they aren't just delaying things, but they're actively exploiting the gaps in our system? It's like they know exactly where the cracks are and they just keep poking at them. It feels very calculated, almost like they're working in tandem with the \"glitches\" in our own internal processes to stay just under the radar.\n\nHow can we address that kind of systematic exploitation? Is there a way to include language that covers these \"cracks\" or \"vulnerabilities\" they might use to undermine us, so they can't claim they were just following the letter of the law?",
